    description: "FOUND 2026-10-03 by the WI-fahod premise audit; reproduced at dev 3abedae588.\n\nDEFECT. In JS/TS a bare call `helper(p)` where the CALLER'S OWN FILE declares a top-level `helper` binds to ANOTHER file's `helper` at 0.85 (`ast_call_direct`). Under both ES-module and CommonJS scoping, a bare identifier is the innermost binding: a local, the file's own module-scope declaration, an import, then a global. Only a non-module browser script shares top-level names across files, and even there the caller's own declaration is the one in scope.\n\nREPRO (two files, each `function helper(p){return p}` plus a caller):\n- No package.json: `a.js:f -> b.js:helper` and `b.js:g -> b.js:helper`.\n- With a package.json at the root: `a.js:f -> a.js:helper` and `b.js:g -> a.js:helper`.\nEither way one of the two callers is bound to the wrong file. The audit's 6-file JS/TS fixture (.js/.mjs/.cjs/.jsx/.ts/.tsx) bound all six callers to `i.cjs:helper`.\n\nMECHANISM (packages/hypergumbo-lang-mainstream/src/hypergumbo_lang_mainstream/js_ts.py, bare-identifier arm ~5503-5560):\n1. named-import disambiguation (`_disambiguate_by_import`);\n2. `_same_package_candidate` (~820) returns the FIRST candidate under the caller's nearest package.json root, with no same-file preference; it returns None when no package.json exists;\n3. `resolver.lookup(func_name, caller_path=...)`: core symbol_resolution uses caller_path ONLY for test-path filtering, not for proximity.\nNo step consults the caller's own file. The same arm is reached at ~6064 (second `_same_package_candidate` site); check it too.\n\nFIX DIRECTION. Before any repo-wide lookup, resolve a bare name against the caller's own file's module-scope declarations (and let a local/param shadow skip resolution, which `_is_shadowed_by_param` already does). Go's analogue was fixed by WI-bivin (cbb41dbdbb, PR #1383: \"resolve a bare identifier in the caller's own package\"); JS has no package scope, so the file is the unit. Do NOT key the enclosing declaration by name (INV-mozas/INV-midag: position, never name).\n\nACCEPTANCE. The two-file fixture above, with and without package.json: each caller binds to its own file's helper. A caller in a file that does NOT declare helper keeps today's behaviour. Run on one real JS repo and diff the calls edge set by call site (not the count); read a random sample of the changed edges.\n\nRELATED: WI-fahod (same arm, unresolved bare names emit nothing), WI-bivin (Go analogue, done), INV-fahub (magnet deferral in the same arm)."  # 8410
    fields: {}  # 8410
